From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:26:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: sunxi_wdt: let the watchdog core serve timeouts
 above 16 s

The timer counts at most 16 s, and the driver gives this limit as
max_timeout, so the watchdog core rejects every longer timeout with
-EINVAL. systemd asks for 10 minutes for its reboot watchdog by
default. On the -EINVAL systemd-shutdown logs

  Failed to set watchdog hardware timeout to 10min: Invalid argument

and disarms the watchdog, so the rest of the shutdown runs without one.

Give the limit as max_hw_heartbeat_ms instead. The watchdog core then
accepts longer timeouts and pings the hardware in between until the
timeout set by userspace has expired. sunxi_wdt_set_timeout() programs
at most 16 s and keeps the requested timeout, as
Documentation/watchdog/watchdog-kernel-api.rst describes for such
drivers.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S (Allwinner A733) at reboot.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: a 40 s timeout is now accepted, and the
watchdog armed with it resets the board at its end, not after 16 s.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
index 3db34524ed13..a19bd28e0a50 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -166,16 +166,18 @@ static int sunxi_wdt_set_timeout(struct watchdog_device *wdt_dev,
 	struct sunxi_wdt_dev *sunxi_wdt = watchdog_get_drvdata(wdt_dev);
 	void __iomem *wdt_base = sunxi_wdt->wdt_base;
 	const struct sunxi_wdt_reg *regs = sunxi_wdt->wdt_regs;
+	unsigned int hw_timeout = min(timeout, WDT_MAX_TIMEOUT);
 	u32 reg;
 
-	if (wdt_timeout_map[timeout] == 0)
-		timeout++;
+	if (wdt_timeout_map[hw_timeout] == 0)
+		hw_timeout++;
 
-	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.timeout = timeout;
+	/* The watchdog core pings in between for timeouts above 16 s. */
+	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.timeout = max(timeout, hw_timeout);
 
 	reg = readl(wdt_base + regs->wdt_mode);
 	reg &= ~(WDT_TIMEOUT_MASK << regs->wdt_timeout_shift);
-	reg |= wdt_timeout_map[timeout] << regs->wdt_timeout_shift;
+	reg |= wdt_timeout_map[hw_timeout] << regs->wdt_timeout_shift;
 	reg |= regs->wdt_key_val;
 	writel(reg, wdt_base + regs->wdt_mode);
 
@@ -309,7 +311,7 @@ static int sunxi_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.info = &sunxi_wdt_info;
 	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.ops = &sunxi_wdt_ops;
 	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.timeout = WDT_MAX_TIMEOUT;
-	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.max_timeout = WDT_MAX_TIMEOUT;
+	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.max_hw_heartbeat_ms = WDT_MAX_TIMEOUT * 1000;
 	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.min_timeout = WDT_MIN_TIMEOUT;
 	sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.parent = dev;
 
